<title>USA: US Home Builders-Market Index rose to 54 in Feb.</title>
<headline>US Home Builders-Market Index rose to 54 in Feb.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Association of Home Builders said its Housing Market Index rose two points to 54 in February from 52 in January.</p>
<p>Builders' ratings of single-family home sales remained unchanged at 55 in February.</p>
<p>Meanwhile, traffic of prospective buyers jumped six points to 46 in February from 40 in January.  And the component index for single-family sales in the next six months rose to 68 from 63 during the same period.  </p>
<p>A Housing Market Index over 50 generally means the number of positive responses received from builders exceeded the number of negative responses.  The February index is based on the ratings of 380 respondents.</p>
